This is genuinely one of the best games I've played in years.
If you like Game of Thrones, buy this.
If you like complex, twisting, winding stories, buy this.
If you like playing games where choices matter, buy this.
If you don't like realistic depictions of medieval warfare (and other things that I won't spoil), buy this but don't play it in a darkened room/before bed.
In short, buy this game. It is AMAZING.
(I'll try not to spoil anything, but if I do then I apologise)
Good:
- Actual actors from the show reprise their roles - Cersei, Tyrion, Jon, Margaery, Daenerys, they're all here;
- Actual music from the show (including the opening credits/intro - it's an exact replica of the TV show);
- Fantastic graphics. Some of the artwork is hand drawn, and it shows. It's beautiful;
- A genuinely interesting, well written, complicated story that keeps you guessing until the very end;
- House Forrester are a family you very quickly care about;
- Some very interesting, well thought out, well designed side characters;
- Your choices matter. You might not think they do when you make them, but further down the line, they will do. And they may not have the result you initially anticipated. This ain't no Mass Effect "stock up them paragon points" game.
- VERY replayable. (I plan on having multiple save files available for when Season 2 is out)
Bad (I say bad, this is me being VERY picky):
- Story can be a bit disjointed in places (but it does mostly tie together at the end);
- It ends on a cliff hanger, which is fine, but doesn't give much closure on anything. Season two HAS been announced, but still, you get no closure whatsoever, which is a little disappointing.
- Some characters you might expect to pop up, don't;
- Ramsay Snow gave me nightmares for about a week.
- You'll probably see the words Valar Morghulis quite a lot, until you get the hang of the rather unforgiving combat.

