A Fistful of Gun (AFoG) is a crazy yet beautiful shooter that is very clearly a labor of love.
AFoG adds charm to a mostly over-saturated genre, you are given a roster of 11 characters to choose from, each boasting unique weapons and a different play style which means everyone should be able to find a character that fits into their preferences. AFoG throws you into crazy large gun battles and at times it can be really intense watching your last friend trying to clutch. With up to NINE player co-op, you and your friends and your friends friends can all team up. Heck, there is even deathmatch, you and your friends can find out who is the real AFoG champ. Additionally, badass music (WHICH YOU CAN BUY
) and awesome pixel art show how much work went into this title.

A cheap, enjoyable RPGMaker made experience that can be bought for 5 bucks, or if you wait for a sale, 19 cents!
Pros:
- Easily obtainable achievements;
- Interesting take on the history side!;
- Replayability, due to the existence of 3 different endings;
- Every object has a description!
Cons:
- No voice acting;
- Low resolution, some crashes and freezes;
- Not recommended for gamers that don't enjoy RPGMaker made games.
Not really much to speak of, just ponder your purchase using these aspects :D
PS: Don't blink!

